      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i've been seeing some stuff in older study guides about how different groups respond differently to meds or even how they perceive pain, which seems wild but i know some of those old studies are still cited. do you think there are any significant biological or physiological differences in how common conditions like cardiovascular issues or even just basic pain sensitivity manifest across different races?",
